        "name": "Kṣemarāja",
        "text": "Kṣemarāja explains that deep sleep, while peaceful, is not the goal. It is a state of pure non-discrimination — but not the supreme non-discrimination that comes from recognizing the unity of all things. Rather, it is the non-discrimination of obscuration: nothing is distinguished because awareness has been temporarily withdrawn.\n\nThis is precisely the operation of māyā: the cosmic power that obscures distinctions and unities alike. Deep sleep, on this analysis, is a microcosm of māyā — and recognizing this is essential to understanding the structure of bondage."
