        "text": "Lakshmanjoo emphasizes the difference between sauṣupti (deep sleep) and samādhi. Both are states of apparent silence. But in sauṣupti, the silence is the silence of unconsciousness; in samādhi, the silence is the silence of intensified, undivided consciousness. The yogi must learn to distinguish these two infallibly."
