        "name": "Abhinavagupta",
        "text": "Abhinavagupta develops Umā extensively in the Mālinīvijaya-vārtikā and the Parā-trīśikā-vivaraṇa. The goddess Parā is identical with the supreme power of will, and her appellation as Kumārī indicates that she is prior to all particular cognitions and actions. She is the originating spark, the first throb (spanda) of consciousness's self-differentiation."
