        "text": "Kṣemarāja explains this sūtra as describing one of the most striking accomplishments of the advanced practitioner. Once immersion in the depth has been established (3.16), the practitioner discovers the power to manifest their own world — to cause the appearance of experiences that conform to their own intention.\n\nHe emphasizes that this is not magical thinking but a recognition of how consciousness actually works at the highest levels. At the level of supreme awareness, consciousness is not the passive recipient of an externally-given world; consciousness is the source of the world.\n\nKṣemarāja further notes that this teaching must be understood carefully. The advanced practitioner does not manipulate the gross physical world by mere thought; they participate consciously in the supreme creative activity that manifests the world as a whole."
