        "name": "Kṣemarāja",
        "text": "Kṣemarāja explains that this sūtra describes one of the most beautiful aspects of the realized practitioner: their function as a cause of knowledge in others. The practitioner who is firmly established in the supreme Self becomes, by their very presence, a doorway through which others can also access this recognition.\n\nHe emphasizes that this function is not performed deliberately as a teaching activity (though it may also be expressed in formal teaching). It operates simply by the practitioner's being. Their established recognition radiates outward and awakens corresponding recognition in those who are ready.\n\nKṣemarāja further notes that this teaching describes the actual mechanism of guru-disciple transmission. The genuine teacher does not transmit information primarily; they transmit a quality of recognition, which can be received by the student who is open to it."
