        "name": "Abhinavagupta",
        "text": "Abhinavagupta develops this teaching extensively in his Tantrāloka. He emphasizes that the capacity for cosmic creation is one of the natural expressions of supreme realization, but he carefully limits its scope.\n\nHe further argues that this capacity should not be sought as a goal. The practitioner who pursues this capacity directly will not develop it; the practitioner who is solely oriented toward supreme recognition will find that this capacity arises naturally as one of its fruits."
