        "text": "Kṣemarāja explains that this sūtra addresses an important epistemological question. How does the practitioner know that they have the capacity for cosmic creation described in 3.36? The answer: through their own direct experience. This is not a doctrine to be accepted on authority; it is a capacity that becomes evident in one's own experience as the path progresses.\n\nHe emphasizes that this is consistent with the broader Kashmir Śaiva approach to knowledge. The supreme realizations of the path are not matters of doctrinal assent but of direct experiential recognition. The practitioner does not believe themselves to have certain capacities; they experience these capacities operating.\n\nKṣemarāja further notes that this teaching protects against false claims. Practitioners who claim such capacities without the corresponding direct experience are revealing their failure to understand the teaching."
