        "name": "Kṣemarāja",
        "text": "Kṣemarāja explains that this sūtra extends the principle of awareness-continuity from the previous sūtra into a different dimension. Just as awareness is maintained across the three states (3.38), so it is to be maintained across the various levels of manifestation: the inner mind, the body, the senses, and the external objects of perception.\n\nHe emphasizes that this is a comprehensive integration. The advanced practitioner does not maintain awareness only in inner contemplation while losing it in bodily activity or outer engagement. They maintain it across all levels of manifestation.\n\nKṣemarāja further notes that this teaching reinforces the integration of inner and outer that runs throughout the chapter. There is no privileged location for awareness; awareness operates equally in mind, body, senses, and external world."
