        "text": "Bhāskara emphasizes the climactic character of this sūtra. After many sūtras describing partial attainments, this sūtra names the complete liberation: the full dissolution of the limited self.\n\nHe notes that this dissolution is described in present-life terms. The practitioner becomes a jīvanmukta — a liberated being while still alive. The dissolution is of the limited self-identity, not of physical existence."
